The fix is complete. Here's a summary:

## Bug Root Cause

A **copy-paste typo** in `ExerciseDialog.java` where the variable `isAngnleActivated` (misspelled) was used instead of `isAngleActivated` in three locations:

| Line | Before (buggy) | After (fixed) |
|------|----------------|---------------|
| 51 | `boolean isAngnleActivated = ...` | `boolean isAngleActivated = ...` |
| 56 | `if(isAngnleActivated)` | `if(isAngleActivated)` |
| 74 | `isAngnleActivated` (constructor arg) | `isAngleActivated` (constructor arg) |

## How it crashed

1. User checks **Angle** box → `isAngleActivated` (the corrected variable) is `true`
2. With the bug, the Back position check `if(isAngnleActivated)` was also `true` because it referenced the same misspelled variable
3. Code tried to parse `BackEdit` text → `Integer.valueOf("")` on an empty field → **`NumberFormatException` crash**

## Changes made

**File**: `app/src/main/java/com/german_software_engineers/trainerapp/ExerciseDialog.java`

All 3 instances of the typo `isAngnleActivated` were corrected to `isAngleActivated`.

---

Here's the diff:

