## Bug Analysis

**Root cause**: A typo in `ExerciseDialog.java` where `isAngnleActivated` was used instead of `isAngleActivated` in three locations:

| # | Location | Bug |
|---|----------|-----|
| 1 | Line 51 | Variable name `isAngnleActivated` (local, functional but wrong) |
| 2 | Line 56 | `if(isAngnleActivated)` — this was supposed to be `if(isBackActivated)`, causing BackEdit parsing to trigger when Angle was checked, crashing on empty text via `NumberFormatException` |
| 3 | Line 74 | `Exercise` constructor argument passed `isAngnleActivated` instead of `isAngleActivated` |

**Crash flow**: User checks Angle box → the Back condition incorrectly references the same typo'd variable → if Angle is checked but Back text is empty → `Integer.valueOf("")` → `NumberFormatException` → crash.

